@* Every icon in the admin. SOLID — one filled path per glyph, no strokes.

   Filled marks hold their weight beside NRT far better than 1.5px outlines did: at 16-18px an
   outline icon next to Kurdish text reads as a faint sketch, while a solid one reads as a peer.
   It is also what the reference uses.

   Directional glyphs get Mirror="true", which flips them with rtl:-scale-x-100. Never mirror a
   clock, a play triangle, a checkmark or a magnifier: only arrows and chevrons carry direction. *@

<svg class="@Class @(Mirror ? "rtl:-scale-x-100" : "")"
     viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"
     aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    @((MarkupString)Path(Name))
</svg>

